Rule for faults "Payment fault handling". Handle ["provider unknown" by "Fault handling"]. End policy.
Scope "Fault handling" within "Payment".
Start at "Inspect history".
Inputs empty. Outputs empty. Outcomes ["complete"].
Use cancellation "Stop work", faults "Unhandled faults", closure "Ordinary close" and races "Acceptance order".
Receive fault history from "Payment history" and record in "Fault history".
Keep "Fault history" as type "Provider fault history" from "History types" under "Expense access".
Sensitivity "expense". Purposes ["Reimbursement"]. Participants ["Employee", "Manager", "Finance reviewer", "Payment operator", "Clock observer"].
Capabilities ["Check the claim", "Create the payable", "Notify the employee"]. Invalidate ["Inspect history"]. Initially unavailable. End data.
Keep "History copy" as type "Provider fault history" from "History types" under "Expense access".
Sensitivity "expense". Purposes ["Reimbursement"]. Participants ["Employee", "Manager", "Finance reviewer", "Payment operator", "Clock observer"].
Capabilities ["Check the claim", "Create the payable", "Notify the employee"]. Invalidate empty. Initially (the value of "Fault history"). End data.
Let "History has expected type" mean ((field "type" of (the representation of (the value of "Fault history"))) equals ("provider unknown")) as truth value with parameters empty.
Step "Inspect history". Choose by ["expected" when "History has expected type"]; otherwise "unexpected". On "expected", continue with "Done". On "unexpected", continue with "Done". End step.
Step "Done". Finish as "complete".  End step.
End scope.
